{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>As its principal.</b> That is the קֶרֶן — the principal of the money." "<b>And a fifth of it.</b> The Torah multiplied many fifths for a single principal: if he denied the fifth and swore, then confessed, he again brings a fifth upon that fifth, and so it continues adding until the principal sworn about diminishes to less than the value of a perutah (Bava Kamma 103)." "<b>To him to whom it belongs.</b> To him whose money it is (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:08.597544656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}